  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  version: \"2.0.1\"\n\npackage:\n  name: nanoflann\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://github.com/jlblancoc/nanoflann/archive/${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: bb3991ad924248d3f20953a951c34878196c11ca112d800acc341c3808443896\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - cmake\n    - ${{ compiler('cxx') }}\n    - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n    - if: unix\n      then: make\n  # The nanoflann library is header only, so we do not need\n  # to export the compiler run-time libraries.\n  # They are just needed during the build to perform some checks.\n  ignore_run_exports:\n    from_package:\n      - ${{ compiler('cxx') }}\n      - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n\ntests:\n  - package_contents:\n      include:\n        - nanoflann.hpp\n      files:\n        - if: unix\n          then:\n            - share/cmake/nanoflann/nanoflannConfig.cmake\n            - share/cmake/nanoflann/nanoflannConfigVersion.cmake\n            - share/cmake/nanoflann/nanoflannTargets.cmake\n            - lib/pkgconfig/nanoflann.pc\n          else:\n            - Library/share/cmake/nanoflann/nanoflannConfig.cmake\n            - Library/share/cmake/nanoflann/nanoflannConfigVersion.cmake\n            - Library/share/cmake/nanoflann/nanoflannTargets.cmake\n            - Library/lib/pkgconfig/nanoflann.pc\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://github.com/jlblancoc/nanoflann\n  license: BSD-2-Clause\n  license_file: COPYING\n  summary: A C++ header-only library for Nearest Neighbor (NN) search wih KD-trees\n  description: |\n    nanoflann is a C++ header-only library for building KD-Trees, mostly optimized\n    for 2D or 3D point clouds. nanoflann does not require compiling or installing.\n    You just need to #include <nanoflann.hpp> in your code.\n  documentation: http://jlblancoc.github.io/nanoflann/\n  repository: https://github.com/jlblancoc/nanoflann\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - sea-bass\n    - tadeu\n    - jlblancoc\n    - jschueller\n",
